{"result": "For TDSR, we calculate it as the Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI) plus an additional housing-related debt component based on property ownership: if the customer owns property, we add the monthly mortgage balance (annual mortgage balance divided by 12) divided by monthly income; if the customer rents, we add the rent payment divided by monthly income; otherwise, no additional component is added. The average TDSR is then computed across customers in each segment.

Regarding the grand total: the "All Segments" row is produced as a rollup across all segments, but it is subject to the same exclusion rule (segments with 10 or fewer customers are excluded from the aggregation), so it reflects only the customers in the included segments. The final ordering is by average TDSR descending, which means the "All Segments" row is sorted together with the other segments rather than being forced to the last position.

